

                   ADVENTURER-KINGS:  GAME 3, TURN 6

                                  FOR

                                 CIRCE







          Marco Calabresi
          
              
                              




  Quote of the Week:

  John II, King of Poland, after routing the Turks from Vienna in 1683 A.D.:
  "The immortal God... has blest us with so signal a victory as scarce the 
memory of man can equal.  Thanks be to Heaven, now the Half-Moon triumphs no 
longer over the Cross!"


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:


  In spring, Hecate cast a spell giving magical powers of oratory to Circe.
  Circe moved into Chirfa (#603) with her army.  Viewing the eastern 
horizon, a man can see a Plain province called Limerick (#703).  It is said 
that Kwoth reigns there.  It is known to be occupied by Orcs.  Their Orcish 
warriors traditionally array themselves as Phalanx.  Southeast of here lies 
the rich province of Ngara (#604), ruled by 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll.  It is known to be a Jungle province 
inhabited by Humans.  Their Human warriors array themselves as Legion and 
Light Cavalry.

  A fleet of ships carried the banner of Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango 
(#0) into the Sea province of the Fourth Sea, ruled by Circe.  Alain (#33)'s 
forces conquered the Fourth Sea without any major engagements.  Alain leads 
approximately 1 Phalanx, 1 Legion, 4 Dragons and 2 Trolls.
  The wet spring was followed by early summer.  Circe cast a spell giving 
magical powers of oratory to Circe.

  Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0)'s forces initiated a campaign of 
conquest directed at the Silver Sea, a Sea province owing allegiance to 
Circe.  Alain (#33)'s forces experienced little resistance in the Silver Sea 
and Alain there established our reign.  Alain leads approximately 1 Phalanx, 1
Legion, 6 Dragons and 2 Trolls.

  Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0)'s minions initiated a campaign of 
conquest directed at the Flying Fish Sea, a Sea province owing allegiance to 
Circe.  Tlazolteotl (#88)'s forces took the Flying Fish Sea without any 
major battles.  Tlazolteotl leads approximately 1 Phalanx and 2 Dragons.
  Midsummer's night passed and a pleasant late summer came.  Circe moved 
into Limerick (#703) with her redoubtable army.  Northeast of here lies the 
province of the Daedalus Sea (#702), ruled by Kwoth.  It is said to be a 
Plain province occupied by Orcs.  Their Orcish fighters traditionally fight 
in the style of Phalanx and Fleet.  To the east lies a Desert area named 
Gafsa (#803), populated by Humans.  It is ruled by Kwoth.  Their Human 
fighters prefer to fight as Camel Corps.  Turning to the southeast, one can 
see a Desert area, which is known as Tebessa (#704).  It is populated by 
Humans and Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll rules there.  Their Human 
warriors prefer to fight as Legion and Heavy Cavalry.

  A fleet sent by the empire of Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0) 
entered the Hammerhead Sea, hoping to conquer that province ruled by Circe 
and made up of great Seas.  Alain (#33)'s naval forces took control of the 
Hammerhead Sea practically uncontested.  Alain leads approximately 1 Phalanx,1
Legion, 3 Dragons and 2 Trolls.

  Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0) ordered an invasion force into the 
adjacent Sea province of Oceanus Acidium, owned by Circe.  Tlazolteotl (#88)
's forces encountered little resistance in Oceanus Acidium and Tlazolteotl 
there established our reign.  Tlazolteotl leads approximately 4 Phalanx and 3
Dragons.
  The summer surrendered to the fall.  Circe cast a spell giving magical 
powers of oratory to Kwoth (#3).
  Tornadoes sucked up the 20th Legion in Limerick and destroyed them.  
Tornadoes sucked up the 21st Light Cavalry in Limerick and destroyed them.  
Tornadoes sucked up the 22nd Legion in Limerick and destroyed them.  
Tornadoes sucked up the 246th Camel Corps in Limerick and destroyed them.  
Tornadoes sucked up the 343rd Bowmen in Limerick and destroyed them.
  Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0) sent an invasion force into the 
adjacent Desert province of Siouxhome, owned by Circe.  Alain (#33)'s armies 
took control of Siouxhome practically uncontested.  Alain leads 
approximately 1 Phalanx, 1 Legion, 5 Dragons and 3 Trolls.

  Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0)'s minions initiated a campaign of 
conquest directed at the Crab Sea, a Sea province owing allegiance to Circe. 
Tlazolteotl (#88)'s forces experienced little resistance in the Crab Sea and 
Tlazolteotl there established our reign.  Tlazolteotl leads approximately 4 
Phalanx and 5 Dragons.
  With the coming of the early winter season, Khalturin was devastated by an 
earthquake!  Circe tried to improve her Tactics, but the task seemed beyond 
her natural ability.


  Soldiers carrying the battle-standards of the Babba Sissoko (#0)ian empire 
marched on the Plain province of Rosehaven, a land garrisoned by the forces 
of Circe.  Tlazolteotl (#88)'s forces took Rosehaven without any major 
engagements.  Tlazolteotl leads approximately 3 Phalanx and 3 Dragons.
  Circe's forces fought in a battle in Limerick, but a foreign general 
commanded it.  The battle is in the General Intelligence Report.
  Thus endeth the adventures of Circe for this year.


  Circe treated with her ally Bradipo I (#2).  Circe treated with her ally 
Kwoth (#3).  Circe treated with her ally Hokuto (#4).  Circe treated with 
her ally Prometeo (#5).  Circe treated with her ally Kahn (#6).  Circe 
treated with her ally Giovanna d'Arco (#7).  Circe treated with her ally 
Agesilao (#9).
  Your Majesty, I have news to report of wanderers in our kingdom:  
  Jolin (#37) rode into Big Sky in search of adventure.
  Tilden (#47) arose one day with a desire to see Kaluga, and so left from 
Khalturin to journey to that province.
  Attla (#54) grew tired of Silvermist and left for Balmwood.
  Ashley (#74) has just recently wandered into Balmwood from St Helens.
  The 213th Chariots lost hope of finding adventure in Silvermist, and so 
they mustered their strength and moved on to Chirfa.
  The 278th Fleet experienced a hard winter in the Mirkwood Sea and sank to 
Depleted quality.  The 278th Fleet laid down their swords and quit the 
mercenary life.


  Here is the financial report for Circe's kingdom: this turn, the Kingdom 
collected 35 gold in revenue.  24 gold was expended to finance our leaders.  
The 178th Garrison and the 179th Garrison trained well and improved in 
quality.  9 gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Circe was left with 5 
gold in the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Behemond
To: Circe

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the advent of the spring season, I prepared to quench my thirst for 
adventure.  I tried a Bless spell, but botched it.
  In early summer, I moved into Siouxhome.  While adventuring, I encountered 
no monster.
  Midsummer's day passed and a hot late summer arrived.  I journeyed to 
Kerry.  During my travels this season, I was approached by a 
Giant Praying Mantis.  Casting a Mirror-Image Phantasm spell, I channelled 
glowing, interlacing strands of magic and an illusion of 
the Giant Praying Mantis sprang into existence!
  The Giant Praying Mantis loped along smoothly and closed to bow range.
  The mirror illusion of the Giant Praying Mantis rushed into melee combat.  
The Giant Praying Mantis lunged at the image of the Giant Praying Mantis and 
damaged the illusion of the Giant Praying Mantis, inflicting 2 damage 
points.  The illusion of the Giant Praying Mantis then snapped at 
the Giant Praying Mantis and inflicted 6 damage points on 
the Giant Praying Mantis.  The Giant Praying Mantis attacked the illusion of 
the Giant Praying Mantis but its aim was just off the mark.
  Undaunted, the mirror illusion of the Giant Praying Mantis moved in and 
lunged at the Giant Praying Mantis and walloped the Giant Praying Mantis 
with 2 damage points.  The Giant Praying Mantis whirled around and snapped 
at the mirror image of the Giant Praying Mantis and scored on the illusion 
of the Giant Praying Mantis, doing 5 points of damage.  The illusion of 
the Giant Praying Mantis lunged at its enemy and inflicted 5 damage points.  
The Giant Praying Mantis fell, fatally injured.  The illusion switched 
targets and now attacked its master.
  The mirror image of the Giant Praying Mantis charged into melee range.  I 
disbelieved the illusion of the Giant Praying Mantis and it gradually faded 
away.  I killed the Giant Praying Mantis while the Giant Praying Mantis was 
in its unconscious state.  I could not locate any magical treasure.

  While speaking to some locals, I heard a rumor about a Dungeon in Tebessa 
(#704), occupied by the Chimera.  Some maintain that the Chimera owns the 
Book of Druidic Incantations.
  The summer surrendered to fall.  I was tutored in Spying by Helatia.  I 
practiced my Spying and improved substantially.
  With the coming of the early winter season, I was tutored in Spying by 
Helatia.  I practiced enthusiastically and improved my skill in Spying.

  Thy humble servant,   Behemond


From: Duqaq
To: Circe

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I travelled to the Albatross Sea.  Viewing the eastern horizon, 
a man can see a Mountain province known as the Iceberg Sea (#808).  It is 
said that Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango is the ruler there.  It is known 
to be occupied by Humans.  Their Human fighters array themselves in the 
style of Legion and Chariots.  Southeast of here lies the province of the 
Sirius Sea (#809), ruled by Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango.  It is known 
to be a Mountain province occupied by Humans.  Their Human fighters fight in 
the style of Axemen and Heavy Cavalry.
  Windy spring was followed by early summer.  I couldn't recruit Phalanx and 
Phalanx in the Albatross Sea because there wasn't enough gold.  So, I really 
tried hard to improve my Druidism, but I practiced in vain.
  With the advent of the late summer season Duqaq's attempted cast of the 
Clairvoyance spell was unsuccessful.  A mysterious magical aura may have 
worked against my spell.
  In fall, Duqaq's Illusory Terrain spell backfired and I wound up with my 
face covered with psycho-kinetic slime.
  The fall season darkened into early winter.  I tried a Bless spell, but 
botched it.

  Thy humble servant,   Duqaq


From: Helatia
To: Circe

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the spring season, I set out to quench my thirst for 
glory.  I failed in my attempt to cast a Bless spell.
  During early summer, I rode into Donegal.  While adventuring, I saw no 
monster.
  Midsummer's night passed and a hot late summer arrived.  I moved into 
Kerry.  During my travels this season, I was stopped by a patrol.  Their 
commanding officer suspiciously challenged me.  But I was obviously no 
outlaw, and that got me off the hook.

  With the advent of the fall season, I really tried hard to improve my 
Spying, but I practiced in vain.
  During early winter, I worked hard on my Spying but was frustrated in my 
self-improvement efforts.

  Thy humble servant,   Helatia


From: Jamielle
To: Circe

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Winter melted into spring.  I cast a Phantasmal Armies spell and illusory 
armies were formed for Alexius.
  With the advent of the early summer season, I was instructed in the art of 
Marches by Alexius.  I practiced my Marches and improved noticeably.
  Midsummer's night passed and a hot late summer came.  I tried to improve 
my Illusions, but the task seemed beyond my aptitude.
  With the advent of the fall season I tried to improve my Illusions, but 
the task seemed beyond my natural aptitude.
  With the coming of the early winter season I tried to practice my 
Illusions, but the task seemed beyond my aptitude.

  Thy humble servant,   Jamielle


From: Gridley, Squire to Philo
To: Circe

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the advent of the spring season, Philo set out to quench his thirst 
for glory.  He sailed into the Constitution Sea (#609) with his formidable 
forces.  To the south, the landscape is scarred by an unending expanse of 
frigid ice.
  The Constitution Sea was conquered by Philo's fleet.  The Constitution Sea 
was found to have an income of 0 gold.
  The wet spring was followed by a fragrant early summer.  Philo moved into 
Mare Atlasta (#709) with his Fleet.  To the south icy wastes extend to join 
the far horizon.

  Soldiers carrying the battle-standards of the Circeian empire marched on 
the Mountain province of Mare Atlasta, a land defended by the soldiers of 
Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0).  Philo commanded the invading armies. 
The defenders were commanded by Thorus (#45).  The armies were drawn up into 
lines of battle as shown here:

