  DEFENDING ARMY

  The defenders had the 138th Warg Riders, the 307th Garrison and the 308th 
Garrison in reserve.  Philo led his armies into the battle.  Thorus marched 
with his loyal troops, jaws set in grim determination.
  The Skeletal Armies led by Babba Sissoko (#0) marched into battle with a 
fanatical fervor.  Philo was unlucky, for he couldn't locate a protected 
encampment to rest his troops, thus his men were in poor condition.  Also, 
in spite of his industrious planning, he was tactically outfoxed and 
realized that this affair was becoming an uphill struggle.

  Across the whole front, the 338th Fleet Marines were arrayed against the 
Crack 236th Warg Riders.  The 338th Fleet Marines battled the 236th 
Warg Riders and had their booties kicked all the way up their throats.
  The host of Thorus (#45) crushed the army of Circe's fighting spirit with 
one last push.  The 236th Warg Riders scattered the 338th Fleet Marines in 
all directions.  The 237th Warg Riders gave chase and annihilated the 339th 
Fleet Marines.
  Philo's armies were defeated and pushed out of Mare Atlasta.  His forces 
completely destroyed, Philo fled alone to the Constitution Sea.
  With the coming of the late summer season, Philo could find no soldiers in 
the Constitution Sea for the requested Light Cavalry troops.  Instead, Philo 
practiced his Meleeing well but could not improve his Meleeing.
  In fall, Philo cast a Illusory Terrain spell and the Mountain terrain of 
Mare Atlasta was magically made to appear as Sea.
  In early winter, Philo cast a Bless spell.  Khalturin was magically 
blessed and prospered.  The Bless affected no armies in Khalturin.

  Thy humble servant,   Gridley, Squire to Philo


From: Hecate
