  Thy humble servant,   Hecate


From: Reynald
To: Circe

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the advent of the spring season, I prepared to quench my thirst for 
adventure.  I recruited a rough force of mercenary ships in the Crab Sea who 
call themselves the 58th Whales.
  The wet spring was followed by a fragrant early summer.  I disbanded the 
58th Whales, the 336th Light Cavalry and the 337th Light Cavalry.
  In late summer, I travelled to Oceanus Acidium.
  With the advent of the fall season I rode into the Balearic Sea.
  The fall cooled into early winter.  I moved into the Third Sea.  Turning 
