  Thy humble servant,   Gunga Din, Squire to Alexius


From: Geoffrey
To: Circe

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the spring season I prepared to quench my thirst for 
glory.  My Clairvoyance spell fizzled and I wound up with my face covered 
with psycho-kinetic slime.
  The wet spring blossomed into a fragrant early summer.  I moved into 
Balmwood.  During my travels this season, I encountered a Renegade Swordsman.
Incanting a Telekinetic Storm spell, I directed glowing, writhing strands of 
magic and damaged the Renegade Swordsman, scoring 12 damage points.  
The Renegade Swordsman staggered, stunned by the mortal blow.  I could not 
find any magical artifacts.  I took the treasure chest that once belonged to 
the Renegade Swordsman.  I located a treasure of 1 gold.

  With the coming of the late summer season, I practiced my Meleeing 
diligently for months, but could make no headway.
  In fall, I was instructed in Psychic Magic by Hecate.  I practiced my 
Psychic Magic and improved noticeably.
  The fall season cooled into early winter.  I was instructed in the art of 
Psychic Magic by Hecate.  I practiced enthusiastically and improved my 
ability in Psychic Magic.

  Thy humble servant,   Geoffrey


From: Eric
To: Circe

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the spring season I set out to quench my thirst for 
adventure.  I directed the 66th Garrison to remain in Big Sky with Alexius.
  I heard a rumor telling of a feature in Kilkenny (#801), a Petrified 
Forest inhabited by the Gryphon.  The Petrified Forest is reputed to contain 
the Large Hoard of Gold.
  In early summer, I travelled about Big Sky, exploring its features.  After 
my exploration efforts, 89% of it has been explored to date.
  Midsummer's night came and went and late summer came.  I moved into 
Transylvania.
  With the advent of the fall season I journeyed to Abu Matariq.  To the 
northwest there is a Desert province known as Bam Yanga (#105), a land of 
Humans where Giovanna d'Arco rules.  Their Human fighters prefer to fight as 
Camel Corps.  I discovered a feature in Abu Matariq: a Catacombs (#85) 
inhabited by the Hydra.  Legend says the Longbow of Accuracy is hidden here. 
The Hydra is a powerful reptilian monster with many snake-heads which 
inhabits swamplands.  I discovered a heretofore unknown Tower (#113) in Abu 
Matariq, inhabited by the Witch.  Legend says the Large Hoard of Gold is 
hidden here.  The Witch is a horribly ugly hag capable of strong and evil 
magic.
  With the coming of the early winter season I informed me that I was no 
longer an useful asset to the King, and relieved me of my duties.

  Thy humble servant,   Eric


From: Frodo, Squire to Aegir
To: Circe

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, Aegir announced a plea for volunteers in Big Sky and was able 
to form the 178th Garrison and the 179th Garrison to fight for Alexius.
  In early summer, Aegir rode into Transylvania.
  With the advent of the late summer season Aegir travelled to Kiska.
  The summer mellowed into a colorful fall.  Aegir journeyed to Jadegate.
  During early winter, Aegir canned Aegir, saying to him that Aegir "was no 
longer worth his salt".

  Thy humble servant,   Frodo, Squire to Aegir


