IMPERIAL OFFICE REPORT

  Into thy heroic dreams cometh an apparition heaven-sent, to speak to thee of
thy progress in thy ambitions for Imperial Office.  It is not for mortal Kings
to know who rivals them for high offices, but the Divine One will allow you to
know thy place in the standings, and how thee compares to thy fiercest foreign
rival for each office (shown under "Riv%" as a percentage: your points divided
by your rival's points, times 100.)

Imperial Office           Best Hope     Rank  Riv%   Second Hope   Rank  Riv%
World Emperor             Circe            5    31   None
Esteemed High Chancellor  Reynald         21    27   Behemond        31    18
Imperial Treasurer        Circe           10     7   None
Imperial Grand Marshal    Circe            1   105   None
  As Circe reviewed her troops in parade, she was startled by the sudden 
appearance of a Silver Baton in her right hand.  A gruff voice which only 
Circe seemed to hear commanded, "You are to have the guardianship of this 
Marshal's Silver Baton, handed down from the Imperial Grand Marshals of the 
Ancient Dynasty who kept order in the Empire untold years ago, in an 
almost-forgotten era.  It will allow you to recruit one extra unit of any 
army type which can move overland (except for flying units).  For example, 
if a province has Legion and Chariot army types, you may recruit two of each 
type.  The Baton cannot be transferred, and will remain yours only for as 
long as you remain the world's greatest general".

