GENERAL INTELLIGENCE REPORT

Kingdom of Babba Sissoko (#0):
  In fall, the Mountain terrain of Mare Atlasta was magically made to appear 
as Sea.

  In early summer, Thorus (#45) marched into Mare Atlasta from the Albatross 
Sea to defend Mare Atlasta against its would-be conquerors.
  In early winter, Tlazolteotl (#88) flew over to Rosehaven.
  In spring, Alain (#33) flew into the Fourth Sea.
  In early summer, Alain flew over to the Silver Sea.
  In late summer, Alain flew into the Hammerhead Sea.
  In fall, Alain flew over to Siouxhome.

Kingdom of Uga-Buga Makumb (#1):
  In late summer, Chaco was hit by a plague.
  In fall, Uga-Buga Makumb (#1) flew into Jerbilia.
  A conquering horde owing their allegiance to 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll invaded the province of Jerbilia, a 
Desert area owned by Kwoth (#3).  Jerbilia was conquered and occupied by 
Uga-Buga Makumb (#1)'s host.
  In early winter, Uga-Buga Makumb flew into Chaco.
  A host of warriors carried the banner of 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll into the Plain province of Chaco, ruled 
by Kwoth (#3).  Uga-Buga Makumb (#1) commanded the attacking armies.  The 
defenders were led by Hokuto (#4).  Uga-Buga Makumb (#1)'s campaign effected 
the conquest of Chaco.


Kingdom of Bradipo I (#2):
  In spring, in Kiska, Bradipo I (#2) campaigned against the provincial 
Eagle chieftain.  Bradipo I commanded the invading armies.  The defenders 
were led by the provincial Eagle chieftain.  Kiska was overrun by Bradipo I
's men in a bloody campaign.

Kingdom of Kwoth (#3):
  In late summer, Chaco was hit by a plague.

  In fall, a conquering horde owing their allegiance to 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll (#1) invaded the province of Jerbilia, a 
Desert area owned by Kwoth (#3).  Jerbilia was conquered and occupied by 
Uga-Buga Makumb (#1)'s host.
  From Circe:  In early winter, Limerick was magically flooded.
  Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll ordered an invasion force into the 
adjacent Plain province of Limerick, owned by Kwoth (#3).  Teleko (#72) was 
in command of the invading armies.  The defenders were led by Kwoth (#3).  
The armies were drawn up into lines of battle as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of Limerick (0703):

 319th/A   322nd/A   323rd/V   326th/A   321st/A   320th/A  
  Eagles    Eagles    Trolls   Dragons    Eagles    Eagles  
 |||01|||  |||01|||  |||01|||  |||01|||  |||01|||  |||01||| 
------------------------------------------------------------
 |||03|||  |||03|||  |||03|||  |||03|||  |||03|||  |||08||| 
 261st/A    15th/A   234th/C   235th/A    67th/V    26th/A  
 Phalanx   Phalanx    Legion    Legion    Legion    Weres   
                                                            
  DEFENDING ARMY

  Teleko (#72) led his armies boldly into the battle.  Kwoth (#3) stood 
determinedly at the head of his thousands.  Circe led a host of loyal 
soldiers into the battle.
  Teleko (#72) strode forward and challenged Kwoth (#3) to personal combat.  
Kwoth answered the challenge to honorable combat.  Lifting his hands high in 
the air, Teleko cast a Spiritwrack spell, to make Kwoth quake and shiver 
with spiritual convulsions.  Kwoth advanced to bow range.  Waving his hands, 
Teleko orchestrated supernatural forces of magic, casting a Holy Symbol 
spell.  A golden mist in the shape of a cross formed around Teleko.  Kwoth 
charged into the melee.  Showing no fear, Kwoth moved closer and swang at 
Teleko and inflicted 3 damage points on Teleko.  His spell was disrupted by 
the event.  Kwoth swang at Teleko but his aim was slightly off the mark.  
Teleko violently attacked Kwoth but Kwoth evaded the blow.  Kwoth deftly 
swang at Teleko and would have hit Teleko if Teleko hadn't ducked just then. 
Teleko forced back Kwoth with his spirited assault.  Teleko then thrust at 
Kwoth with terrific strength but his sword whiffed harmlessly through the 
air.  Teleko swang at Kwoth and missed badly.  Kwoth maneuvered for a good 
attacking vantage.  Then Kwoth swang at Teleko with all his might but his 
aim was just off the mark.  Kwoth thrust at his nemesis but Teleko dodged 
the sword.  Hoping to take advantage of a gap in Kwoth's defenses, Teleko 
thrust at Kwoth and scored on Kwoth, doing 2 points of damage.  Kwoth 
daringly swang at Teleko and would have hit Teleko if Teleko hadn't ducked 
just then.  With surprising speed, Teleko thrust at Kwoth and damaged Kwoth, 
inflicting 5 damage points.  Teleko swang at Kwoth and scorched Kwoth with 2 
damage points.  Kwoth feigned retreat, then whirled and thrust at Teleko and 
inflicted 3 damage points.  Teleko violently assailed Kwoth and inflicted 5 
damage points on Kwoth.  Kwoth staggered, stunned by the force of the mortal 
blow.  Thus did Kwoth finally die, a defiant death by any standard.  The 
forces commanded by Kwoth were disheartened by his death, yet still they 
moved ahead with some hope of victory.  Circe assumed command of the forces 
of the realm of Circe.  An unfavorable omen manifested itself, which of 
course dealt a severe blow to Teleko (#72)'s hopes.  Teleko's mount was shot 
and killed while Teleko was giving a speech.  On the other hand in this 
perilous slugging match, Teleko appeared to have the tactical edge.
  The Dragons commanded by Teleko were not impressed by his lack of 
leadership ability.  Kwoth (#3) gave a rousing harangue to his troops, which 
bolstered their courage.  Circe started with a rousing harangue to her army, 
which bolstered their courage.  The Werefolk led by Circe were disgusted 
with her lack of leadership ability.
  On the right wing, the 319th Eagles faced the 261st Phalanx.  The 319th 
Eagles swooped down on the 261st Phalanx and attacked without mercy.  On 
this field, scouts of the 319th Eagles had been trapped before the battle.  
They were killed and their bodies catapulted over the 319th Eagles.  This 
goaded the 319th Eagles into a berserk attacking rage.
  But the battle was not yet over.  The 261st Phalanx's opponents were 
overjoyed when a beautiful golden eagle flew overhead, a wonderful omen.  
But their joy turned to despair when a boorish soldier killed the bird (a 
SURE sign of doom!)  The 319th Eagles fought the 261st Phalanx and battled 
them tooth and nail, neither side willing to give ground.
  Within the interior lines, the 322nd Eagles faced the 15th Phalanx.  The 
322nd Eagles swooped down on the 15th Phalanx and attacked without mercy.  
In this match, the men of the 322nd Eagles ran into some unpredictable 
footing and were afflicted with great disruption.  The 322nd Eagles fought 
the 15th Phalanx and could not hold their ground against their savage foe.
  In the interior lines, the Veteran 323rd Trolls were arrayed against the 
Crack 234th Legion.  In this area, many men of the 323rd Trolls were 
suffering from hangovers, weakening their fighting strength significantly.  
The 323rd Trolls battled the 234th Legion and could not quite hold their 
ground against their savage opponent.
  Within the interior lines, the 326th Dragons faced the 235th Legion.  The 
326th Dragons fought with the 235th Legion and could not stand their ground 
and executed an orderly retreat.
  Within the interior front, the 321st Eagles were arrayed against the 
Veteran 67th Legion.  The 321st Eagles swooped down on the 67th Legion and 
attacked them.  Here, some of the 67th Legion had been drawn off by the need 
to take a small but centrally situated castle, so they were far below their 
usual strength.  Still, the 321st Eagles battled with the 67th Legion and 
could not quite hold their ground against their determined foe.
  On the left wing, the 320th Eagles faced the 26th Were-Beasts, who were 
stiffened by a tough outfit of freedom fighters of the Mercenaries Guild, 
who led them into a fanatical fervor by example of their fearless elan.  The 
320th Eagles swooped down on the 26th Were-Beasts and attacked without 
mercy.  Here, the musicians of the 26th Were-Beasts bravely volunteered to 
march in the van, and all the soldiers were stirred by their spirited 
singing.  The 320th Eagles battled the 26th Were-Beasts and battled them to 
a standstill.
  Circe's great horde overwhelmed the army of Uga-Buga Makumb (#1) and took 
the field, scattering their enemies.  Though Circe's forces were triumphant, 
Teleko (#72) rallied his men and decided to contest Limerick.

Kingdom of Hokuto (#4):
  In fall, Hokuto (#4) moved into Balmwood (#503) with his redoubtable army.
  In early winter, Hokuto boldly marched his forces into Chaco (#504).
  A host of warriors carried the banner of 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll (#1) into the Plain province of Chaco, 
ruled by Kwoth (#3).  Uga-Buga Makumb (#1) commanded the attacking armies.  
The defenders were led by Hokuto (#4).  Uga-Buga Makumb (#1)'s campaign 
effected the conquest of Chaco.
